# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state — NEVER commit. This is not just clutter, it is a privacy leak.
#
#   cache.json  contains one entry per transcript file, and those paths encode
#               every project/client/job directory name you have worked in.
#   config.json contains your calibration samples, i.e. your actual usage levels.
#   state.json  contains derived spend figures.
#
# All three live in ~/.claude/usage-budget/ (or $USAGE_BUDGET_HOME) by design,
# outside this repo. These patterns exist to catch a stray copy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cache.json
config.json
state.json
*.json.tmp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Agent tooling scratch. `.claude/worktrees/` is where Claude Code puts throwaway
# git worktrees; committing it would nest checkouts of this repo inside itself.
# Note this ignores any *local* .claude/ — if a shared agent config is ever added
# here deliberately, unignore it explicitly rather than dropping this line.
.claude/

# Demo fixture — regenerated by claude-code/demo/fixture.py. Synthetic, but it
# is still a transcript tree and a state dir, and those are exactly the shapes
# this file exists to keep out of the repo. Only the rendered GIF is committed.
claude-code/demo/fx/

# Scratch
/tmp/
*.log
